# Runs of tests/fixtures/text_in_place.neo: workers, then mode a b. Build with NEO_ALLOC_STATS=1.
# Each text is built in place and again a byte at a time; the run prints its length and checksum when they are equal.
# Numbers as parts: the edges of each digit count, negatives, a last part that is a number, hexadecimal digits sliced from a literal.
1	0 0 0		=446 531113348 OK\n
1	0 5 0		=450 567669671 OK\n
1	0 123456 0		=473 930791813 OK\n
# A page of rows: functions that end in a concat, a loop that builds its text, a let named where it is read.
1	1 0 0		=16 764487795 OK\n
1	1 1 0		=132 274798383 OK\n
1	1 7 3		=577 182696361 OK\n
1	1 1000 17		=78791 89910212 OK\n
4	1 1000 17		=78791 89910212 OK\n
# html_escape as a part: every length up to a, the five bytes at moving places, every byte value.
1	2 0 1		=575 615962172 OK\n
1	2 40 1		=10690 316041725 OK\n
1	2 70 9		=30598 822789035 OK\n
# Texts that share a base, hand a part on, or are changed after they are built.
1	3 0 0		=OK\n
1	3 7 0		=OK\n
1	3 1234567 0		=OK\n
1	3 -5 0		=OK\n
# The word pattern: the first b bytes of a word; more than eight, or fewer than none, traps as the slice does.
1	4 7523094288207667809 0		=<>0\n
1	4 7523094288207667809 1		=<a>1\n
1	4 7523094288207667809 5		=<abcde>5\n
1	4 7523094288207667809 8		=<abcdefgh>8\n
1	4 7523094288207667809 9		!byte slice bounds
1	4 1 -1		!byte slice bounds
# A page of a rows makes at most 24 allocation requests: no row, number or escaped text has a buffer of its own.
1	5 1000 17		=78791 89910212 OK\n
1	5 3000 5		=240041 692869508 OK\n
# Small texts whose parts are the last uses of their buffers, 200,000 rounds: the resident set does not grow.
1	6 200000 0		=52166400 OK\n
# Fragments joined by halves, as they are and with their parts: the same text, and at most 32 allocation requests to join them.
1	7 0 0		=19 252204252 OK\n
1	7 1 3		=334 439207423 OK\n
1	7 5 2		=1190 953816616 OK\n
1	7 1000 17		=242052 38319436 OK\n
# html_escape of texts known at build time (literals, an if between literals, functions that only return literals) and of one that is not.
1	8 0 0		=0 7 OK\n
1	8 1 0		=54 671598529 OK\n
1	8 37 0		=2208 145102444 OK\n
